diff --git a/docs/reference/errors.mdx b/docs/reference/errors.mdx
index 58170a6..26bb952 100644
--- a/docs/reference/errors.mdx
+++ b/docs/reference/errors.mdx
@@ -92,8 +92,8 @@ These appear in terminal output and in the report as plain string codes.
 | `APP_URL_REQUIRED` | A navigation or relative URL on a target that declares no `app.url`, or an `app.command` with no `app.url` or `app.readyUrl` to poll | configuration | 2 |
 | `INVALID_APP_URL` | Base URL with userinfo, a query, a fragment, a non-HTTP scheme, plain HTTP on a non-loopback host, port 0 on a host other than a literal loopback address (`127.0.0.1`, `[::1]`), a loopback address the run could not bind a free port on, or unparseable | configuration | 2 |
 | `INVALID_GLOB` | Empty pattern, a first segment that starts with `!` beyond the one leading `!` of a `tests` exclusion (`!!tests/**`, `./!tests/**`), a bare `!`, braces, character classes, extglobs, a backslash separator, an absolute path, a `..` segment, a trailing `/` or `.`, a `tests` entry with no wildcard that names a directory (the message names the glob to write), a pattern that names only the project root, or a `**` that is not a whole segment | configuration | 2 |
-| `UNKNOWN_TARGET` | `--target` named an ID that is not configured | configuration | 2 |
-| `TARGET_REQUIRED` | `e2e mcp`: the config declares several targets and neither `--target` nor `open_session` named one | configuration | 2 |
+| `UNKNOWN_TARGET` | `--target`, `open_session.target`, or `openHost` (`e2e/runner`) named a target that is not configured | configuration | 2 |
+| `TARGET_REQUIRED` | `e2e mcp` or `openHost` (`e2e/runner`): the config declares several targets and none was named | configuration | 2 |
